WEBVTT

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:06.420
This is a pile of sheets full of counts. In about a minute it's going to write a sentence that is not in this book.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:19.840
Each row is a word from a book, and the words that came next, with a mark every time. Maybe you did the counting yourselves; maybe the sheets arrived finished. It works the same either way.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:34.700
Every box has a colour, always in the same order: red, blue, green, yellow. On this row, red means "magpie". On another row, red means something else.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:49.560
A story starts after a full stop, so find the row for full stop. Fill a cup with one counter for every mark: seven red for "it", four blue for "here", three green, three yellow.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:01:07.560
Seventeen counters. Which colour do you reckon we're most likely to draw? Now draw one without looking. Red: "it". Write the word down, empty the cup back into the tub, and go to the row for "it".

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:16.500
The row for "it": three red, three blue, three green, one yellow. Red again: "sits".

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:24.040
"Sits" is only ever followed by "on", and "on" by "the". One box, no cup.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:40.260
The row for "the" fills the cup with all four colours. Yellow: "dog". And after "dog", two red for a full stop, two blue for "runs". Red: full stop.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:46.600
The book says "It sits on the fence". We've ended up with "It sits on the dog".

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:58.460
After "the", we could pick "magpie", "fence", "postie" or "dog". These four branches show those choices; a thicker branch means more counters.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:05.680
Another go might take a different branch, or pick "dog" again. Repeats are part of the activity.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:18.260
Claude or ChatGPT also generates text by repeatedly predicting what comes next. It learns those predictions differently, using much more context than our last word.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:36.280
Four jobs in your group. A reader finds the row. A filler puts one counter per mark in the cup. A drawer pulls one out. And a writer writes the word down. Empty the cup back into the tub every time.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:41.560
Reader, find the full stop. Let's see what your book says.
